A final STEP 0 audit has uncovered a disqualifying shortcut, so I’m reversing the build rather than shipping a false Track B claim. Because each eight-entry source signature contains an odd (hence invertible) residue, a solver can match that one anchor against the four odd residues in each target and test at most 12 multipliers. That is under roughly 109 modular operations—comparable to, and often shorter than, the claimed invariant route. The family therefore fails H on both tracks.
